hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-8 : List (List Word)
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-8 = cons "Every major design (RDF and the semantic web stack, OWL and description logics, property graphs, Wikidata, the" (cons "industrial graphs of search engines, knowledge-graph embeddings, and lately retrieval layers built over language" (cons "models) delivers some of these and patches the rest from outside. The patches are well known: reification and" (cons "RDF-star for statements about statements, named graphs for provenance, SHACL for constraints, `owl:sameAs` and" (cons "ontology-alignment systems for identity, materialization jobs for inference, and versioning schemes for change." (cons "Each patch adds a layer, and each layer has its own semantics, which the others don't respect." (cons "" (cons "The argument here is that the five promises aren't five features. They are five aspects of one object, and a" (cons "graph whose elements are that object keeps all five by construction." (cons "" nil)))))))))
